From 070a80fb1281afe12f74d4e63a8f40e95d304a8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 15:32:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 876/913] plat-stm32mp1: scmi: replace assert-only realloc
 check with real check
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

assert() compiles to a no-op when NDEBUG is defined, so
assert(plat_protocol_list) in add_protocol() did not protect against
a failed realloc() in release builds, letting the code write to
plat_protocol_list[plat_protocol_list_count - 1] through a NULL
pointer.

Replace the assert() with an explicit NULL check that panics.

Coverity issue: CID 1200768: CERT-C POSIX
Coverity issue: CID 1200780: CERT-C Error Handling

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 3caa7dfa8cd764a9dba3f030485730d191e1e49c plat-stm32mp1: scmi: replace assert-only realloc check with real check]
Assisted-by: GitHub-Copilot:Claude-Sonnet-5
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I33bb26029a74e10a43e968219fe8f26c12f2c942
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/592856
Domain-Review: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
---
 core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/scmi_server.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/scmi_server.c b/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/scmi_server.c
index d62bfccfd..22db26633 100644
--- a/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/scmi_server.c
+++ b/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/scmi_server.c
@@ -306,7 +306,8 @@ static void add_protocol(uint8_t protocol_id)
 	plat_protocol_list = realloc(plat_protocol_list,
 				     plat_protocol_list_count *
 				     sizeof(*plat_protocol_list));
-	assert(plat_protocol_list);
+	if (!plat_protocol_list)
+		panic();
 
 	plat_protocol_list[plat_protocol_list_count - 1] = protocol_id;
 }
